---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro"
import Header from "../layout/Header.astro"
import Footer from "../layout/Footer.astro"
import { DEFAULT_DISTRO, href, type DistroId } from "../../lib/flavor"

interface Props {
	distro?: DistroId
}

const { distro = DEFAULT_DISTRO } = Astro.props
const repo = "https://github.com/LevitateOS/LevitateOS"
---

<BaseLayout distro={distro} canonicalPath="/licenses/" title="Licences · LevitateOS" description="The licences of LevitateOS and AcornOS: our own code, the third-party software in the ISOs, and how to get the source of the GPL and LGPL programs." preloadDisplay={false}>
	<Header distro={distro} />
	<main id="main" class="wrap">
		<div class="story-section prose">
			<p class="eyebrow">Last updated November 2026</p>
			<h1>Licences</h1>

			<h2>Our own code</h2>
			<p>The source code of LevitateOS and AcornOS (the installer, the rec* tools, Recipe, the build system and this website) is dual-licensed: you may use it under either the <a href={`${repo}/blob/master/LICENSE-MIT`}>MIT licence</a> or the <a href={`${repo}/blob/master/LICENSE-APACHE`}>Apache-2.0 licence</a>. Contributions are accepted under the same terms. The <a href={`${repo}/blob/master/LICENSE`}>LICENSE file</a> in the repository lists the components and their licences.</p>

			<h2>Software from other people</h2>
			<p>The ISOs and the systems installed from them also contain third-party software, each part under its own licence. The Linux kernel is GPL-2.0-only. Much of the rest is under the GPL, the LGPL or other free-software licences such as MIT, BSD and Apache-2.0. LevitateOS's userland is built from Fedora 45 RPM packages and AcornOS's from Alpine Linux 3.24 APK packages, so those packages' licences apply to the programs they contain.</p>
			<p>The licence texts of the installed software are in <code class="inline-code">/usr/share/licenses</code> inside the image. LevitateOS's Fedora packages bring theirs, one folder for each package. Alpine's packages carry only the name of their licence, so AcornOS has one folder for each licence identifier its packages declare (<code class="inline-code">/usr/share/licenses/GPL-2.0-or-later/LICENSE</code>), and <code class="inline-code">/usr/share/licenses/MISSING.txt</code> lists the identifiers whose text it does not carry yet, each with the packages that declare it.</p>

			<h2 id="source">Source code offer</h2>
			<p>For at least three years after the release, on request to the project's issue tracker (<a href={`${repo}/issues`}>https://github.com/LevitateOS/LevitateOS/issues</a>) we provide the complete corresponding source code of every GPL- and LGPL-licensed program in the release on a medium customarily used for software interchange, for no more than the cost of physically performing the distribution. The exact upstream source packages and their hashes are listed in <code class="inline-code">SOURCES.txt</code>.</p>
			<p><code class="inline-code">SOURCES.txt</code> is an asset of each release in <a href="https://github.com/LevitateOS/releases/releases">LevitateOS/releases</a>, next to the ISO. The release build writes it from the locked package lists and lists each source package with its URL and hash.</p>
			<p>The upstream sources are also public: Fedora's at <a href="https://src.fedoraproject.org">src.fedoraproject.org</a> and Alpine's at <a href="https://pkgs.alpinelinux.org/packages">pkgs.alpinelinux.org</a>. The kernel is built from pinned upstream source with the configuration in the repository's <code class="inline-code">distro/variants</code> folder.</p>

			<h2>Privacy and security</h2>
			<p>How this website treats your data is on the <a href={href("/privacy/", distro)}>privacy page</a>. To report a security problem, read <a href={`${repo}/blob/master/SECURITY.md`}>SECURITY.md</a>.</p>
		</div>
	</main>
	<Footer distro={distro} />
</BaseLayout>
